  "name": "Growl Hound",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "Riddim growl: Square Morph one octave above a clean sine sub, 3-voice narrow unison, a one-shot Mod A (1/8, Decay) snapping the Index from narrow pulse back to square on every note, Saturate (2x oversampled at the default quality) into a note-tied Comb- that rings on every third harmonic, then an LP12 the filter envelope opens on the attack. Mod B slowly drifts Motion so repeated notes are never identical. Play: 1/8 and 1/16 call-and-response around F1-C2, mono legato; short notes bark, held notes settle into the metal comb tone. Tweak: Mod A Index amount for bite, Filter A Freq for the metal colour (it follows the note), Shaper Amt for dirt, Filter B Freq for darkness. Macro plan (not wired yet): Growl = Mod A Index amount, Metal = Filter A Freq + Res, Dirt = Shaper Amt, Motion = Mod B Motion amount.",
